# 🔴 THE LOCKFILE IS TRACKED HERE, unlike upstream. Deliberate divergence.
#
#    This project publishes binaries that other people flash onto hardware, so
#    the same tag has to produce the same firmware. Resolving components freshly
#    on every build means a component moving upstream can change what somebody
#    installs without a single commit here - and the failure would show up as a
#    hardware fault on a stranger's desk, not as a build error.
#
#    It is also not hypothetical: a fresh resolve on this machine left
#    espressif/esp_h264 listed in the lock and not installed, which broke the
#    configure with an error about a Kconfig symbol nobody had heard of.
#    `idf.py update-dependencies` settled it.
#
# dependencies.lock   <- intentionally NOT ignored
.env
releases/
main/assets/lang_config.h
main/mmap_generate_emoji.h
.DS_Store
.cache
*.pyc
*.bin
mmap_generate_*.h
.clangd
